1. Pick up the shopping basket from the entrance.
2. Place the promotional sign near the clothing store.
3. Open the storage room door.
4. Close the display cabinet.
5. Move the shopping cart to the cart collection area.
6. Pick up the customer information brochure from the information desk.
7. Place the lost-and-found box on the customer service counter.
8. Turn off the display screen in the information kiosk.
9. Pick up the shopping basket and place it at the entrance.
10. Open the storage room and retrieve the promotional stand.
11. Pick up the toy box and place it on the display shelf.
12. Retrieve the cleaning supplies and place them in the maintenance room.
13. Open the information desk drawer and collect the mall directory.
14. Pick up the folded wheelchair and place it near the customer service desk.
15. Collect the promotional flyers and place them on the information counter.
16. Pick up the shopping cart and return it to the designated collection area.
17. Go to the supermarket, collect a shopping basket, and return it to the mall entrance.
18. Navigate to the electronics store, retrieve the display stand, and deliver it to the promotional area.
19. Go to the customer service desk, collect the lost-and-found package, and place it in the storage room.
20. Navigate to the bookstore, retrieve the promotional banner, and place it at the main entrance.
21. Go to the food court, collect the tray, and return it to the tray collection station.
22. Navigate to the toy store, retrieve the display item, and place it on the promotional shelf.
23. Go to the maintenance room, collect the caution sign, and place it near the wet floor area.
24. Navigate to the information desk, retrieve the mall directory, and place it inside the kiosk.
25. If shopping baskets are unavailable at the entrance, retrieve additional baskets from storage.
26. If the lost-and-found counter contains an unclaimed package, move it to the storage room; otherwise organize the customer service desk.
27. If the display shelf is full, place the promotional item on the secondary display shelf.
28. If the information kiosk is active, place the mall directory beside it; otherwise return the directory to the information desk.
29. If a shopping cart is left unattended in the corridor, return it to the collection area; otherwise inspect the entrance.
30. If the promotional stand is already installed, organize the remaining promotional materials; otherwise install the promotional stand.
31. If the storage room door is open, close it before returning to the customer service area.
32. Carry the glass display item without dropping or tilting it.
33. Transport the shopping cart without colliding with customers or store displays.
34. Move the promotional stand carefully without blocking emergency exits.
35. Carry the folded wheelchair while keeping it stable.
36. Place the electronic display device on the counter without disconnecting its power cable.
37. Transport the food tray without spilling any beverages.
38. Move the decorative flower pot without damaging nearby displays.
39. Collect all shopping carts from the mall corridors, return them to the designated collection area, inspect the entrance for additional carts, and return to the information desk.
40. Prepare the shopping complex for opening by placing shopping baskets at the entrance, arranging promotional stands, organizing the information desk, and ensuring customer service equipment is ready.
41. Inspect every shopping zone for misplaced shopping carts, promotional materials, unattended baskets, and open storage rooms, correct each issue, and return to the information desk.
42. Restock the information desk by collecting brochures, mall directories, promotional flyers, and lost-and-found forms from storage, arranging them neatly, and returning to the entrance.
43. Collect trays from the food court, return them to the collection station, organize the dining area, inspect the seating area for misplaced items, and return to the information desk.
44. Prepare the mall for closing by collecting promotional materials, organizing shopping baskets and carts, securing customer service equipment, turning off information displays, and returning to the maintenance room.
45. Perform a complete facility inspection by checking store entrances, customer service areas, information kiosks, food court seating, promotional zones, and storage rooms for misplaced items or open equipment, resolve each issue, and return to the customer service desk.
